hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18005","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Shubah, he said: Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me from Hafs ibn Asim from Abu Said ibn al-Mualla, he said: I was praying, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called me and I did not answer him until I had prayed, then I came to him and he said: What prevented you from coming to me. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I was praying. He said: Did not Allah Almighty say: O you who believe, respond to Allah and to the Messenger when he calls you. Then he said: I shall surely teach you the greatest surah in the Quran, or from the Quran, before you leave the mosque. He said: Then he took my hand, and when he was about to leave the mosque I said: O Messenger of Allah, you said: I shall surely teach you the greatest surah in the Quran. He said: Yes, All praise belongs to Allah, Lord of the worlds, it is the seven oft-repeated and the mighty Quran which I was given."
"18006","Abu al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us from Abd al-Malik, meaning Ibn Umayr, from Ibn Abi al-Mualla from his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed one day and said: A man, his Lord Almighty gave him choice between that he live in this world as long as he wishes to live in it and eat in this world as much as he wishes to eat in it, and between meeting his Lord, so he chose meeting his Lord. He said: Then Abu Bakr wept, then the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you not wonder at this old man, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned a righteous man whom his Lord Almighty gave choice between meeting his Lord and between this world, so he chose meeting his Lord, and Abu Bakr was the most knowledgeable of them of what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, then Abu Bakr said: Rather we ransom you, O Messenger of Allah, with our wealth and our sons. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no one among people more generous to us in his companionship and his wealth than Ibn Abi Quhafah, and had I taken a close friend I would have taken Ibn Abi Quhafah, but affection and brotherhood of faith, but affection and brotherhood of faith, twice, and your companion is the close friend of Allah Almighty."
